lass="enc-snip">Hakata is a historic port on Hakata Bay in northern Kyushu, now a ward of the city of Fukuoka.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/hakau"><span class="enc-name">Hākau</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Hākau was ruler (aliʻi nui) of the island of Hawaiʻi around 1500, the son and heir of Līloa.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/hakka-people"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/hakka-people.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Hakka people</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Hakka are a Han Chinese people whose ancestors migrated in waves from northern China to the hill country of Guangdong, Fujian and Jiangxi, keeping a distinct Hakka…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/hakodate"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/hakodate.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Hakodate</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Hakodate is a port city in southern Hokkaido, Japan, on the Tsugaru Strait.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/hakon-eiriksson"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/hakon-eiriksson.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Håkon Eiriksson</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Håkon Eiriksson was the last Earl of Lade, a grandson of Håkon Sigurdsson.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/hakon-grjotgardsson"><span class="enc-name">Håkon Grjotgardsson</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Håkon Grjotgardsson was a Norwegian chieftain from Hålogaland in the late 9th century, the founder of the line of the Earls of Lade.</span></a></li></ul>
